info title=The Stalker's Hollow
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A cavern under the trench lip, 40 m down: four alcoves of air round an arena, a seal valve on a plinth, the Network gate - and the Abyssal Stalker. The tenth island of The Sunken Kingdom, the end of its finale.
island on.arrive=message||A buoy, and a chain going down past the trench lip. A teal glint far below - or a lamp.

story stalkerhurt|Stalker wounded|Scrap|You wounded the Abyssal Stalker - it called the small ones.
story stalker|Abyssal Stalker|Scrap|You drove off the Abyssal Stalker.
story valve|Seal valve turned|Hinge|You turned the seal valve in the Hollow.

note wardenentry Warden's last entry | WARDEN'S LOG - LAST ENTRY - G. FENNICK\n\nIt hunts by the lamps. Keep to the alcoves - it can't get its head in.\nWhen it's hurt it calls the little ones. Don't stay out in the open then. The floodlights round the hollow are the only thing it is afraid of; turn them on it while it is calling.\nThe valve on the plinth answers the Spire. Whatever gets pulled up there, the valve finishes it down here.\nThe Director came down the chain an hour after me, with a lamp. First sensible thing he has done in nine years. We are going to the vent together to wedge it while the big one sleeps.\nIf you are the Stalker: I did say. Several times. In writing.
note ringwavenote What the Ringwave means (part 1) | Scratched into the plinth's brass plate:\n\nTHE RING IS THE SEA. THE THREE WAVES ARE THE THREE LAYERS IT WAS BUILT TO MOVE.\n\nThe rest of the plate has rusted through.
note lastrestore The last word | RESTORED.\n\nThe gate under the Ringwave stands open, the alcoves glow teal, and somewhere far up the cable the pumps are running. Up the trench, the Commons' great doors are open and four hundred people are walking into the light.\nBy the vent, in the silt: a warden's whistle, a burnt-out lamp, two sets of footprints going in and none coming out.\nOn the cable radio, Ines: "Lights all the way to the roofs. Milo's plane landed. It's coming up with us, so we'll keep the floodlights on. Bring Mo home."
note lastseal The last word | SEALED.\n\nThe stone plug sits over the gate, and the Hollow is quiet. The Network's lamps will go out one by one, and the Commons will live on in the dark, safe and very quiet, for as long as dark lasts.\nBy the vent, in the silt: a warden's whistle, a burnt-out lamp, two sets of footprints going in and none coming out.\nOn the cable radio, Ines: "It's dark. It's quiet. Halvard got what he wanted, in the end. I'll go up the lift to Milo. Bring Mo home."

