note sh_cavechest Stalker's hoard | Things the Stalker dragged in: a diver's tank, a lamp, a broken bag.
loot sh_cavechest OxygenBottle*1;TitaniumOre*2;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop sh_cavechest loot.refill=0
note sh_ruinnote Watchers' post log | WATCHERS' POST - LOG\n\nWe watched the Hollow for the Network. The Stalker comes up the trench at night and goes back at dawn, like a commuter.\nIt keeps out of strong light - not dim lamps, those it likes, it comes to them like a moth. Strong light, the floodlights, burns it.\nThe old valve in the trench shuts the vent it breathes from.\nLast night two men went past the post towards the vent: a warden in a big coat with no hat, and the Director himself, carrying a lamp. The warden was talking the whole way. The Director was listening. We have never seen him listen.
note sh_wrecknote Boat's last log | BOAT'S LAST LOG\n\nWe came over the trench lip to see the Hollow lit - the Spire had set its fuses, and the whole sea could see.\nThe Stalker came up under us and took the hull like a dog takes a slipper. The crew swam for the post. I stayed with the boat, because somebody should, and because I can't swim, which I have never told anybody.\nI watched it go back down to the Hollow afterwards. It went straight past the lamps and lay down in the dark by the vent, the way you'd lie down by a fire.
note sh_wreckcrate Boat's locker | The boat's locker: titanium, rope, a lamp in oilcloth.
loot sh_wreckcrate TitaniumIngot*1;Rope*3;Bolt*2;Copper*2
prop sh_wreckcrate loot.refill=0
prop shlamp1 beh.repel=8
prop shlamp2 beh.repel=8
prop shtrenchdark zone.radius=9
prop shtrenchdark zone.hazard=dark
prop shtrenchdark zone.hazardMsg=The trench is pitch dark. A headlight would show the valve.
note gatecache Network gate cache | Behind the Network gate: the last keepers' cache, left for whoever opened the way.
loot gatecache TitaniumIngot*3;Battery*2;CopperIngot*2
prop gatecache loot.refill=0
prop sealcache obj.name=sealcache
prop sealcache beh.hidden=1
note sealcache Sealers' cache | The sealers' cache, pushed up out of the floor when the plug came down: what the Network kept for the day it was closed for good.
loot sealcache TitaniumIngot*3;Battery*2;CopperIngot*2
prop sealcache loot.refill=0
prop gate if.use=signal|hollowgate
prop gate else.use=message||Barred from inside. The seal valve opens it - if the Spire chose RESTORE.
# --- DEEP 1-HOUR (10-24): story items, notes and checks
story sh_key|Warden house key|Hinge|The warden house key, from the chest at the bottom of the drowned house.
story sk_crest|Kingdom crest shard|Bolt|A shard of the Sunken Kingdom's crest, from a drowned building. The Hollow's crown vault wants nine.
note shdeep Warden house chest | The wardens' chest: titanium and the last crest shard.
loot shdeep story:sk_crest*1;TradeToken*2;TitaniumOre*2;Bolt*3;OxygenBottle*1
prop shdeep loot.refill=0
note shlocker Lip rock locker | The wardens' locker on the lip rock: spare tanks.
loot shlocker TitaniumIngot*2;MetalIngot*2;Battery*1;Cooked_Potato*2
prop shlocker loot.refill=0
note shsumnote Warden's last card | THE LIP ROCK\n\nWe climbed up here to breathe between watches. From here you see the Spire's lights on the trench, and on a clear night, very far off, the Spirecrest beacon blinking on the roofs.\nThe crown vault in our house wants nine crest shards - one from every drowned building of the kingdom.\nI always meant to bring the boy up here and show him the beacon. Tell him it's not a bad light, just a lonely one. - G.F.
note shbldnote Warden house roll | WARDEN HOUSE - DUTY ROLL\n\nFennick. Fennick. Fennick. (Everyone else went up the lift.)\nThe Stalker hates strong light. Three floodlights stand round its hollow; turn them on it when it is hurt and calling the small ones, and keep to the alcoves between.\nThe crown vault upstairs opens for nine crest shards, one from every drowned building of the kingdom. I put the last one here myself, so that whoever comes all the way down gets something for it.\nIf it is you, Ines: I am sorry about the cage. I am sorry about all of it.
note shledge Watcher's cache | A watcher's cache on the lip rock's shelf.
loot shledge Rope*3;Bolt*2;Feather*3
prop shledge loot.refill=0
note shcave2chest Warden's spare chest | A warden's spare chest in the rock cave.
loot shcave2chest CopperOre*3;Rope*2;Battery*1
prop shcave2chest loot.refill=0
prop shsummit zone.id=sh_summit
prop shsummit zone.radius=2.5
prop shsummit zone.message=Out of the water on the lip rock. Somewhere far below, the Hollow.
story sh_flood|Floodlight on the Stalker|Placeable_Lantern_Metal|A floodlight turned on the Abyssal Stalker.
prop stalker boss.shield=1
prop hfl1 obj.name=hfl1
prop hfl1 beh.use=Turn the floodlight on the Stalker
prop hfl1 if.use=!signal|hfl1
prop hfl1 on.use=signal||hfl1\nhit|stalker|34\ngive||story:sh_flood*1\nmessage||The floodlight blazes into the hollow - the Stalker writhes away from it.
prop hfl2 obj.name=hfl2
prop hfl2 beh.use=Turn the floodlight on the Stalker
prop hfl2 if.use=!signal|hfl2
prop hfl2 on.use=signal||hfl2\nhit|stalker|34\ngive||story:sh_flood*1\nmessage||A second light - the Stalker thrashes in the glare.
prop hfl3 obj.name=hfl3
prop hfl3 beh.use=Turn the floodlight on the Stalker
prop hfl3 if.use=!signal|hfl3
prop hfl3 on.use=signal||hfl3\nhit|stalker|34\ngive||story:sh_flood*1\nmessage||The third light. The hollow is white as day.
note shcrown Crown vault | The crown vault of the Sunken Kingdom, on the warden house's second floor: nine shards of the crest open it.
loot shcrown TitaniumIngot*4;MetalIngot*4;CircuitBoard*2;Battery*2
prop shcrown loot.refill=0
prop shcrown if.open=has|story:sk_crest|9
prop shcrown else.open=message||Nine sockets in the vault's lid, shaped like crest shards. Every drowned building of the kingdom kept one.

quest title=The Deep
quest intro=Fennick and the Director went down to the Hollow. Go down the chain to the trench lip after them.
step reach|lip|1|Go down the chain to the trench lip
step read|Warden's last entry|1|Read the warden's last entry
step read|Watchers' post log|1|Read the log at the watchers' post
step read|Boat's last log|1|Read the last log at the sunken boat
